  "id": "systematic-replication",
  "term": "systematic replication",
  "definition": "Systematic replication is a repeated attempt to reproduce earlier research findings in a planned way, often across several experiments or conditions, to see whether the original effect holds consistently. In the packet, it refers to replication efforts that produced a mix of successful, partial, and failed repeats, used to test whether differences between conditions might explain that pattern.",
